@@@b85e10184efd13b3a7b192de35f80a6ad842ee57	Autoconf fixes2 (#324)	* Port to Autoconf 2.71 (#320)

This is a small set of manual fixes so that Autoconf 2.71
does not complain when one runs 'make -f Makefile.aut'.

* Replace obsolete AC_CONFIG_HEADER with AC_CONFIG_HEADERS.
The latter has been in Autoconf ever since Autoconf 2.50 (2001)
and has long been safe to assume.

* Do not use obsolete AC_HEADER_STDC and AC_HEADER_TIME, which
'less' used only to check for sys/types.h and time.h respectively.
Instead, check for these headers with AC_CHECK_HEADERS, like the other
headers.

* Shrink 'configure'

Use AC_CHECK_HEADERS_ONCE instead of AC_CHECK_HEADERS, to avoid
duplicate checks for the same header.

Remove duplicate AC_TYPE_OFF_T call; once in configure.ac is enough.
configure.ac

