@@@64464509e9dc1b27961744ff72eaedd672e7172c	Restructure edit_ifile(). It now tries to open the new file first, and then if that succeeds, it closes the old (currently open) file. Previously it first closed the current file and then tried to open the new file. If the open failed, it would re-open the old file via reedit_ifile. If reedit_ifile failed, this could cause unintended recursion:	edit_next -> edit_istep -> edit_ifile -> edit_error -> reedit_ifile ->
   edit_inext -> edit_istep -> edit_ifile -> etc.

Besides being ugly, this could crash if edit_istep stored an IFILE
in next=next_ifile(h), and then the edit_ifile(h) deleted (del_ifile)
not just h but also next.

