@@@ae947389c6716386c22a950747fbb864c02e7518	Fix bug introduced in 64464509e9dc1b27961744ff72eaedd672e7172c, where first character of file is not displayed when using LESSOPEN. Since this change, when viewing a new file while another file is already open, the new file is opened first and then the current file is closed. When the new file is opened, open_altfile reads a char from the new file to see if it is empty, and then calls ch_ungetchar to unget it, so that it will later be the first char read from the file. But when closing the old file, close_altfile calls ch_ungetchar(-1) which overwrites the ungotten char. This call was added in 05e12cd1. I'm not exactly sure why it was added, but it seems unnecessary and removing it fixes this problem.	
