@@@c4e2cbaf9b7b13550464082b904b862d099746d7	Update `TH` calls in man pages.	* less.nro.VER:
* lessecho.nro.VER:
* lesskey.nro.VER: Supply date and software release information as
  separate arguments to `TH` macro call.  This causes the page headers
  and footers to be fully populated when using groff man(7) or
  mandoc(1).

Fixes:

$ nroff -ww -t -rCHECKSTYLE=4 -man -z *.nro
an.tmac:less.nro:2: style: .TH missing fourth argument; consider package/project name and version (e.g., "groff 1.23.0")
an.tmac:lessecho.nro:1: style: .TH missing fourth argument; consider package/project name and version (e.g., "groff 1.23.0")
an.tmac:lesskey.nro:2: style: .TH missing fourth argument; consider package/project name and version (e.g., "groff 1.23.0")

Before
======

groff
-----
$ for f in *.nro; do ~/groff-1.23.0/bin/nroff -t -Wbreak -man -T ascii -P -cbou "$f" | sed -n '1p;$p'; done
LESS(1)                     General Commands Manual                    LESS(1)
                           Version 685: 11 Oct 2025                    LESS(1)
LESSECHO(1)                 General Commands Manual                LESSECHO(1)
                           Version 685: 11 Oct 2025                LESSECHO(1)
LESSKEY(1)                  General Commands Manual                 LESSKEY(1)
                           Version 685: 11 Oct 2025                 LESSKEY(1)

(The `-Wbreak` option is to silence a warning regarding an unbreakable
81-character line.)

mandoc
------
$ for f in *.nro; do mandoc -T ascii "$f" | ul | sed -n '1p;$p'; done
