lesskey.nro.VER

@@@5be168c81eeab619d93a56e97468f93550fdf64b	Port use of `\(ha` to AT&T-based troffs.	* less.nro.VER:
* lesskey.nro.VER: Do it.

The `\(ha` special character escape sequence is not portable to
AT&T-based troffs like Solaris 10, Plan 9, and DWB 3.3.

Adapt a technique from ncurses[1] to render the correct character
regardless of formatter.

See groff_char(7) for more background.

Before and after:

Solaris 10 troff
----------------
$ diff -U0 /tmp/less-ha-char-sol10-[12].txt | head -n 11
--- /tmp/less-ha-char-sol10-1.txt       2025-10-11 12:05:01.089695560 -0500
+++ /tmp/less-ha-char-sol10-2.txt       2025-10-11 12:18:05.695348549 -0500
@@ -39 +39 @@
-     In        the  following  descriptions,  X  means  control-X.   ESC
+     In        the following  descriptions,  ^X  means  control-X.   ESC
@@ -47 +47 @@
-     SPACE or V        or f or F
+     SPACE or ^V or f or ^F
@@ -51 +51 @@
-         use V as a special literalization character.
+         use ^V as a special literalization character.

DWB 3.3 troff
-------------
$ diff -U0 /tmp/less-ha-char-dwb-[12].txt | head -n 11
--- /tmp/less-ha-char-dwb-1.txt 2025-10-11 12:03:05.302077033 -0500
+++ /tmp/less-ha-char-dwb-2.txt 2025-10-11 12:17:38.431402954 -0500
@@ -39 +39 @@
-           In the following descriptions, X means control-X.  ESC
+           In the following descriptions, ^X means control-X.  ESC
@@ -47 +47 @@
-           SPACE or V or f or F
+           SPACE or ^V or f or ^F
@@ -51 +51 @@
-                use V as a special literalization character.
+                use ^V as a special literalization character.

Plan 9 troff
------------
$ diff -U0 /tmp/less-ha-char-plan9-[12].txt | head -n 11
--- /tmp/less-ha-char-plan9-1.txt       2025-10-11 12:02:51.194122939 -0500
+++ /tmp/less-ha-char-plan9-2.txt       2025-10-11 12:20:44.562996321 -0500
@@ -41 +41 @@
-         In the following descriptions, haX means control-X.  ESC
+         In the following descriptions, ^X means control-X.  ESC
@@ -49 +49 @@
-         SPACE or haV or f or haF
+         SPACE or ^V or f or ^F
@@ -53 +53 @@
-              use haV as a special literalization character.
+              use ^V as a special literalization character.

...and similarly for lesskey(1), which was using '^' literals.

