@@@890c0ec6b0d8149d995e649597b66e97e577cb57	Revise less(1) synopsis (2/9).	* Stop using groff extension escape sequence `\/` for italic
  corrections, which formats as a slash in Solaris 9, Plan 9, and DWB
  3.3 troffs.  Use man(7) font alternation macros like `IR` and `RI` to
  switch fonts instead; in groff's man(7) implementation, these macros
  supply italic corrections automatically.
* Format ellipses more pleasantly on typesetters by separating their
  dots with thin space escape sequences `\|`.
* Force breaks less often.
* Use `HP` hanging paragraph macro instead of explicit indentation of
  non-initial synopsis lines.
* Save adjustment mode before disabling adjustment, and restore the
  saved mode after formatting unadjusted text.[1]
* Add dummy character escape sequence `\&` after non-terminal ellipsis,
  so that *roff doesn't interpret it as the end of a sentence and supply
  inter-sentence space afterward.

