@@@2ec9af164382c5d49dd6df573fd506bf9ae3984a	less.nro.VER: Obtain formattable `\` correctly.	The sequence `\\` betrays the unwary man page author if used in string
or macro arguments.

groff_man_style(7):
     \e        Format the roff escape character on the output; widely
               used in man pages to render a backslash glyph.  It works
               reliably as long as the “ec” request is not used, which
               should never happen in man pages, and it is slightly more
               portable than the more explicit \[rs] (“reverse solidus”)
               special character escape sequence.

Also drop trailing whitespace from input line to suppress Git complaint.

less.nro.VER

@@@5d8aa263b33e2fca25cc3fdfc6e74ceca41d0859	Access single quote char portably in man pages.	Fixes bad rendering with Solaris 10 and Plan 9 troffs.

