@@@7f8d2c5ff61c1825f878a0c692308c7a173cd609	Missing terminal initialization on empty file.	That pesky a55140f63f409cf0069279a6dbaf2d0ea385a2e5 defers terminal
initialization until the first data byte is received. But if the
input file is empty, there is no first byte so the initialization
has to be done elsewhere. In 5862ab1fd7396e6399ae660f446c4b7cf9fb44a7
term_init is done when iread hits EOF. But in some cases less
decides that a file is empty and never even calls iread.
This adds term_init call to ch_init, when we open an input file
and decide that it's empty.

