@@@30a9914b061015a85d9629626fd2a0b987b9ee6d	Migrate cumbersome URL to groff man `UR` and `UE`.	Format hyperlink to ECMA-48 document using the groff man(7) `UR` and
`UE` extension macros.  If unavailable, the unimplemented macros are
ignored and the link text alone formats.  The only harm done (apart from
the lengthy URL itself not being visibly formatted) is that the period
goes missing from the end of the sentence.  (And even that could be
worked around using conditional requests.  Let me know if interested.)

Quietens a warning (that had to be opted-into) from any groff version.

Fixes:
$ ~/groff-HEAD/bin/nroff -ww -t -r CHECKSTYLE=3 -man -z $(<MANS)
